---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/packmetry-workspace.css';
import '../../styles/examples.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Packing Examples — Packmetry"
  description="Worked Packmetry packing examples based on real benchmark scenarios, canonical metrics and the same verification boundaries used by the product."
>
  <main class="pm-examples-page">
    <div class="pm-examples-shell">
      <header class="pm-examples-hero">
        <p class="pm-example-kicker">
          Packmetry Examples
        </p>

        <h1>
          Worked packing cases,
          with the assumptions visible.
        </h1>

        <p>
          These examples connect real Packmetry
          benchmark scenarios to the measurements,
          result metrics and trust boundaries behind
          a packing decision. They are not templated
          keyword pages or claims of universal
          optimality.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section
        class="pm-examples-library"
        aria-labelledby="examples-library-title"
      >
        <article class="pm-examples-card">
          <div>
            <p class="pm-example-kicker">
              Mixed item sizes
            </p>

            <h2 id="examples-library-title">
              One large item, five small items,
              one carton
            </h2>

            <p>
              Walk through the repository&apos;s
              highly-different-item-sizes benchmark:
              an 80 mm cube plus five 20 mm cubes
              against a 100 mm cube carton, including
              the locked expected outcome and the
              canonical volume-utilization math.
            </p>
          </div>

          <a href="/examples/mixed-item-packing-example/">
            View worked example
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </article>

        <p class="pm-examples-note">
          Future examples should come from real
          benchmark cases, measured product output
          or clearly sourced case studies. Packmetry
          should not manufacture examples simply to
          create more indexable pages.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
